{"from": "artifact:tekhelet-fabrics", "type": "complicates", "to": "claim:mt-09-20-21-fringe", "note": "The ritual identification of murex blue is disputed: 'Others have also disputed that Murex trunculus might not be the correct chilazon due to its failure in fitting many Rabbinic criteria' - so linking the Masada/Murabba'at fabrics to the biblical tekhelet of the tzitzit is contested."}
{"from": "artifact:tekhelet-fabrics", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-tzitzit"}
{"from": "text:hosea-6", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-13-mercy-not-sacrifice", "note": "Hosea 6:6, 'I desire mercy, and not sacrifice; and the knowledge of God more than burnt offerings' - the quotation of 9:13. Cross-reference only; it does not attest."}
{"from": "text:leviticus-24", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-03-scribes-blasphemy", "note": "Leviticus 24:16: 'He who blasphemes the name of Yahweh, he shall surely be put to death' - the Torah law behind the scribes' charge of blasphemy. Cross-reference only."}
{"from": "text:numbers-15", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-20-21-fringe", "note": "Numbers 15:38-39 commands fringes on the garment corners with 'a cord of blue' - the tzitzit of 9:20. Cross-reference only."}
{"from": "text:numbers-27", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-36-sheep-shepherd", "note": "Numbers 27:17: 'that the congregation of Yahweh not be as sheep which have no shepherd' - the shepherd image of 9:36. Cross-reference only."}
{"from": "text:2-samuel-7", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-27-son-of-david", "note": "2 Samuel 7:12-16, Nathan's promise that David's house, throne and kingdom shall be made sure forever - the scriptural background of the title 'Son of David'. Cross-reference only."}
{"from": "text:4q521-2", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-35-teaching-synagogues", "note": "Cross-reference: 4Q521 (pre-Christian Qumran) expects the anointed one to 'proclaim good news to the poor' among his works - the messianic 'good news' idiom of 9:35 (cf. 11:5). A cross-reference only; it does not attest the claim or mark a cell found (link added by review 2)."}
